<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abdallah al-Mahdi Billah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">proclaimed caliph 909</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abdallah al-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahdi">Mahdi</a> Billah was the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimid Caliphate</a>, proclaimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> in 909 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ifriqiya">Ifriqiya</a>. An <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismailism">Ismaili</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imam</a> who claimed descent from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatima">Fatima</a>, the Prophet's daughter, he came to power after the missionary campaign of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-abdallah-al-shii">Abu Abdallah al-Shi'i</a> among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kutama-berbers">Kutama Berbers</a> overthrew the Aghlabid rulers. His proclamation established a Shia caliphate in direct rivalry with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasids</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abdallah-al-mahdi-billah.jpg" alt="Abdallah al-Mahdi Billah" width="320" height="319" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: PHGCOM · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Calif_al_Mahdi_Kairouan_912_CE(png).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 909 his Kutama army overthrew the Aghlabid emirate, and the imam was retrieved from Sijilmasa and proclaimed caliph at Raqqada in January 910 as <b>Abdallah al-Mahdi Billah</b>, establishing a rival caliphate to Baghdad.</blockquote><a href="/empire/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimid Caliphate · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Between about 905 and 909 the future Fatimid caliph <b>Ubayd Allah</b> was held captive there until rescued by Abu Abdallah al-Shi'i, who executed the emir al-Yasa.</blockquote><a href="/state/midrarid-emirate">Midrarid emirate</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in ʻAskar Makram. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahdia">Mahdia</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/tunisia">Tunisia</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=35.51,11.06&amp;year=909" aria-label="Mahdia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4830 881 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the place of death of Abdallah al-Mahdi Billah"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5280 1151h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5280 1151h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the place of death. <a href="/atlas?at=35.51,11.06&amp;year=909">What was here in 909 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
